# What the SDIST carries, which is not what the wheel carries and not
# what setuptools includes by default.
#
# THE DEFECT THIS FILE EXISTS FOR. Without it, the sdist held all 13
# `tests/test_*.py` and none of `tests/conftest.py`,
# `tests/fixtures_time_series.py` or `tests/__init__.py` -- setuptools'
# default sdist rules pick up test modules but not the support beside
# them. Unpacking the released sdist and running `python -m pytest
# tests/` then failed at COLLECTION, on the very command the README
# gives contributors.
#
# It was invisible from every direction already checked: the wheel is
# correct (it ships no tests at all, by design), the emitted tree is
# correct, and `provenance-pool`'s sdist is correct -- but only because
# it has no test helpers for the default rules to miss.
include LICENSE
include NOTICE
include README.md
include pyproject.toml
recursive-include tests *.py
graft renderer
global-exclude __pycache__
global-exclude *.py[cod]
